  "passage": {
    "title": "The Rise of Online Shopping",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Twenty years ago, most people bought their clothes, books and electronics in shops. Today, a large number of us click a button and wait for a delivery. In some countries, more than a quarter of all shopping is now done online, and the number grows every year."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "There are good reasons for this change. Online shops are open twenty-four hours a day, so customers can buy something at midnight in their pyjamas. Prices are often lower than in town, because online companies do not pay for expensive city-centre shops. It is also easy to compare products and read reviews written by other customers before you spend any money."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "However, online shopping has disadvantages. You cannot touch or try on the goods, so about one in five clothing orders is returned because it does not fit. Returning items takes time, and some companies charge for it. Delivery can also be slow or unreliable, and packages sometimes arrive damaged. In addition, many small shops in town centres have closed because they cannot compete, which makes high streets quiet and empty."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "There is an environmental side, too. Delivery vans produce pollution, and online orders often use a lot of cardboard and plastic. On the other hand, one van delivering to fifty homes may cause less pollution than fifty people each driving to the shops. Experts say the effect depends on how customers behave: ordering many items in one go, and not returning goods, helps the planet."
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "Many shops now try to combine both worlds. You can order online and collect the goods in the shop, or try things on in the shop and order a different size online. Whichever way people shop in the future, it seems likely that the high street will change rather than disappear."
      }
    ]
  },
